#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# weber_e

#% text
# `weber_e(nu, z)` gives the Weber function `E_nu(z)`, the integral of `sin(nu*t - z*sin(t))` for `t` from 0 to `pi`, divided by `pi`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 11.10.2. For integer orders it is related to Struve functions, for example `E_0 = -H_0`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
weber_e(0.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.09950754264004316

#% cell
weber_e(1.5, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.10882159808007968

#% cell
weber_e(0, 2.0) + struve_h(0, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The integral definition:

#% cell
n_integrate(sin(0.5*t - 1.0*sin(t)), [t, 0, pi])/pi - weber_e(0.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 2.7755575615628914e-17

